  "findings": [
    "The packaged Firefox GTK3 runtime advertises only the older KDE decoration interface; system preferences alone did not produce a frame with the preceding compositor.",
    "Resolve legacy negotiation by owned surface at commit; xdg-decoration wins if both protocols exist. Both paths share the original frame factory, rendering and input.",
    "Select the browsers existing system-decoration preferences before launching an owned disposable profile; do not patch browser drawing or duplicate controls.",
    "Inventory retains normal frame metrics during fullscreen. Verify actual frame visibility/content bounds and wait for committed client geometry on restoration.",
    "The older frame regression required more than four colors. The preceding compositor also failed it and its whole title RGB equals the new compositor; native bitmap titles legitimately use four grayscale colors."
  ],
